Cambodia's peace is to be kind to each other
Cambodia as a child was different from Cambodia today.
Today, some Cambodians are materialistic, greedy, and deceitful.
According to Meng Ly, the disturbing trend in Cambodia is the tendency of urban dwellers to despise people in rural areas.
Meanwhile, wealthy people have forgotten what they went through.
Born in Battambang in 1969, an area under Khmer Rouge rule and full of massacres and starvation, Mengly felt that his father was lucky to have a child. Eight in different youth groups, because everyone survived, despite all the hardships.
After he was evacuated to a refugee camp in Thailand in 1979, Meng Ly and his five siblings were sent back to Cambodia and then fled to the Khao Khao refugee camp. Idang in 1981.
Finally, in 1984, with the help of the YMCA, all of his family came to the United States, living in Texas and California.
After attending the University of California, he studied medicine at St. Louis University. Lucia and later earned a master's degree in public health from the University of Massachusetts.
Mengly returned to Cambodia in 2002 to work as a public health consultant for an NGO called Health Development Partners, which works on pediatric disease management. .
In January 2005, he founded the Intercontinental School on Mao Zedong Boulevard, then opened the Inter-American Institute at a cost of $ 20,000, which he borrowed from his family.
In his first year, he had only 21 students, and by 2008 that number had grown to 10,000, with both schools becoming the most prestigious schools in Phnom Penh.
The American Intercontinental School currently has 7,000 students, 350 teachers and 700 staff, and six school buildings.
Due to his medical training, Mengly provided health support to students through his clinic.
He said that his school philosophy is a window for students to reflect on the world, focusing on quality, excellence and the future.
Meng Ly is the only child to return to Cambodia.
This really makes him very happy.
We have political stability.
Cambodia is growing and developing rapidly.
For Meng Ly, the most important factor is that the people are becoming more aware and that Cambodia will become part of the ASEAN Economic Community by 2015.
Cambodia should focus on real skills to compete in ASEAN integration and focus on appropriate education, otherwise they will face difficulties.
He said that an important factor for young Cambodians is understanding of the Khmer language, English and information technology.
We need to be able to really communicate both inside and outside the country.
Mengly said Cambodia lacked vocational training in architecture, civil engineering and electrical engineering.
Despite the challenges, Mengly is optimistic that people will show their kindness, as he knew when he was young.
It is not 100% freedom, but you can have freedom of movement and security and political stability.
