Government temporarily suspends imports of frozen goods from India
This measure was implemented on May 1, 2021 until further notice.
Due to the severe situation of Kovid 19 outbreak, the new B1617 source originated in India and in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has temporarily recommended the import of frozen meat and goods. Other high-risk freezes originated in India.
According to the letter of instruction to the director of the branch department and the Office of Customs and Excise dated May 1, the letter also said that the General Department of Customs and Excise also suspended the customs clearance form for those types of goods that arrived at the field. Customs or customs stock already.
The decision to suspend imports came after Commerce Minister Pan Sosak requested permission from Prime Minister Hun Sen on April 30.
In his letter, the minister stated that the seizure of goods already imported and the temporary suspension of imports of frozen meat are in accordance with Article 20 of the General Agreement on Customs and Trade of the World Trade Organization and Article 12. Of the ASEAN-India Commodity Trade Agreement on the basis of urgent public health protection.
The letter added that Cambodia would also conduct research and testing for other viruses, especially coronavirus, on these high-risk meat and frozen products, which would seek cooperation with the Indian government to identify and confirm the virus. Involvement in the production, packaging, freezing and transportation of these products.
In the event that the products are found to be related to the virus 19 Cambodia will take legal action, including the destruction of frozen meat products and frozen goods imported from India, so as to avoid confusion, the Ministry of Commerce will explain to the Indian side. By diplomacy.
Meanwhile, the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO) and the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) have confirmed that there are no data showing that 19 Kovid cases were caused by packaging or frozen meat. China has taken precautionary measures by banning and burning these risky products.
